From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:54:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 120/144] GreatDANE: source-level check that the Dane wordmark
 covers the stock chrome URL (round 4e)

greatdane/tests/wordmark_branding_check.py (no build, no signing, no network) asserts:

- about-wordmark.svg is a plain-text "Dane" wordmark with context-fill, the navy
  #13254A fallback, and a transparent ground, and does not contain the official
  Firefox path-logo.
- content/jar.mn aliases firefox-wordmark.svg to about-wordmark.svg, ships
  about-wordmark.svg, overrides window-firefox.svg to greatdane-icon.svg, and
  keeps the existing sidebar/firefox.svg override.
- There is no differing duplicate firefox-wordmark.svg file.
- Official branding, when present in the tree, still has the upstream Firefox
  wordmark. Stock new-tab / private-browsing CSS, when present, still load
  chrome://branding/content/firefox-wordmark.svg.
- WORDMARK-SOURCES.md documents the stock leftovers that were not swapped, and
  states this is not a trademark clearance.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
